Exploratory analyses for the second review round: the account across writers and classes, out-of-sample baselines and horizon transfer, what binding does to the items a key misses, the zero system after the shift, and why the cited key misses (analysis modules and tests)

Every key starts with explore_; nothing registered changes. ex_account computes the Eq. (1) terms per
writer, class and branch at source-epoch binding and tests the account across cells (Spearman, line,
leave-one-writer-out against the class label); ex_e1_more adds the pooled development cell mean to the
out-of-sample test, the twelve-to-three-month transfer, the missed-item accuracies and the zero system
against HoldMem; ex_misses classifies the changed item-times the cited key missed from the worlds and the
writer's t0 citations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
